# Feature 2299, 2026-11-14: a type qualified by a built-in's name, `sort.Item`,
# with no `use` of the module `lib/sort` that declares it. Defect 2292's
# message offered `use lib/sort`, a `guess` writing a line feature 2299 now
# refuses; and the line with an alias alone would be told again on the
# qualifier it leaves. So the message names the line with its alias and the
# qualifier written with it, and offers no fix. Its first words were *nothing
# named `sort` is in scope*, which a built-in in scope makes false.
function main()
    print(1)

# The value p holds.
function value_of(p: sort.Item) -> i64  #~ unknown_name
    return p.v
